# Experiment protocol: <name>

*How to fill each field, the cuts by tier and the intent ids [C/A/B]:
`protocol-field-guide.md` (`protocol-check --guide`). Fill by label:
`protocol-fill PROTOCOL-<name>.md "<label>" "<value>"`.*

```toml
[protocol]
standard = "0.18"
id = "<protocol-id>"        # stamped by `lib exp`, never typed
type = "<exploratory | confirmatory>"
# exploratory: generates hypotheses, none of it reported as a test;
# confirmatory: tests a hypothesis fixed before the run
cost = "<seconds | minutes | hours>"
# the price of a REPEAT, not whether a model is involved — seconds:
# rerunnable at will, incl. a handful of model calls for a minute and cents;
# minutes: a model pass you would not casually redo; hours: expensive or
# irreversible (→ AS-017 Die Zahl der Audits folgt der Kostenstufe)
frozen = false              # true only after the instrument check
preflight_audit = ""
# date · scope sha · N findings (blockers fixed / accepted with reason /
# dismissed with reason) — the code-vs-intent audit after the instrument
# check, before freezing (→ AS-015 Preflight-Audit vor dem Einfrieren)
```

## Summary † (write last)

- **Result †:** <the answer in at most three plain sentences — the result,
  not the procedure; a limit stands in the sentence it limits; no ids, keys
  or run_ids here, they are in Result below>
- **Question †:** <the question of the Intent, in plain words>
- **Did †:** <what was done, one sentence — for a reader with no context>
- **Status †:** <on track | blocked by <what> | needs a decision on <what>>

## Intent (before the run)

- **Question / hypothesis:** <!-- s --> <the one question — what do we expect?>
- **Success / failure criterion:** <!-- s --> <how do we recognise whether it worked?
  One C per conjunct, each reappearing as a lowercase key in the reportable
  run's metrics.json (→ AS-003 Kein Lauf ohne Intent-Absatz, AS-004 Kennungen machen den Intent adressierbar)>
- **Admissibility condition:** <!-- s --> <what must hold in the same run before
  any verdict is issued — yield, coverage, a control showing its expected
  value; one A per condition; if one fails, there is no C verdict, only the
  finding that the instrument failed (→ AS-004 Kennungen machen den Intent adressierbar)>
- **Registered branch:** <if a result decides the conclusion or the next
  analysis, register it BEFORE the run: condition + what each branch
  licenses, one B per branch point (→ AS-013 Registrierte Weiche, AS-004 Kennungen machen den Intent adressierbar); "n/a" if there is
  only one outcome>
- **Timebox:** <hard budget, e.g. 4h — then log and ask>
- **Split touched:** <which split may be touched: train | dev | test>
- **Why this design †:** <choice of model, dataset, method — one sentence>
- **Rival explanations †:** <per confound: what OTHER than the hypothesis
  produces the same number · error direction (does it push for or against
  the hypothesis?) · the check as CODE in evaluate() (→ AS-044 Der Prüfblick auf einen Konfund ist Code)>
- **Out of scope †:** <the neighbouring questions this run leaves open>

## Result (after the run — write back, don't go quiet)

- **Answer to the question:** <!-- s --> <per registered id its verdict, and the
  run_id; numbers as a small table below the label (one row per arm or
  condition), produced by `analysis/<note>.py --check`, never retyped>
- **Raw output:** <!-- s --> <one real prompt+answer pair per finding>
- **Interpretation / next step:** <one sentence; keep instrument findings
  apart from findings about the subject>
- **Outcome †:** <expected or surprising — failures belong here>
- **Rival check †:** <which rivals are ruled out, which still stand?>
- **Caps/drops †:** <what was omitted or limited>
- **Analysis audit †:** <!-- s --> <date · scope sha · N findings — the audit of the
  EVALUATION against the frozen criterion, before the number leaves; at
  cost seconds due at promotion or when the number steers a decision
  (→ AS-050 Auswertungs-Audit vor dem Berichten, AS-017 Die Zahl der Audits folgt der Kostenstufe)>

